SpesModem: opt-in read-only cellular probe over QMI (boot-arg wwan, default off).

The modem (MPSS.HA.1.1.c1) boots and announces 44 QRTR services, among them DMS 2, NAS 3,
UIM 0x0b, WMS 5, VOICE 9 and WDS 1 (research/live-ram25.txt), but nothing ever talks to them.
This adds a QMI client for DMS, NAS and UIM, the way qmicli does over AF_QIPCRTR (each QRTR
client port is its own QMI client), from new ports 0x4005-0x4007, and logs the answers with
the prefix "SPES WWAN:":

  wwan=1  IMEI (8-digit TAC, rest masked), firmware revision, model, capabilities, operating
          mode, UIM card status (per slot: card state, apps, PIN state), NAS serving system
          (registration, PLMN) and signal info; the NAS pair is repeated every 15 s, 8 times.
  wwan=3  as 1, and if the modem is not ONLINE ask DMS once for ONLINE (radio on, it may then
          register on the network; DMS online mode is not persistent).
  wwan=5/7  as 1/3 with the full IMEI.

Without the boot-arg nothing changes except the names of more services in the existing
"service x:y port z" lines. EFS stays read-only: rmtfs writes are still dropped.
Parsers host-tested with synthetic and truncated replies (ASan/UBSan clean); not built on CI,
not booted.

